/-! # VII-07 (F3b): arbitrary actual Ricci-null pregeodesic fields force `G = 0`

Let `V` be a vector field, `C¹` on an open `U ⊆ esDomain I`, and on all of `U` nonzero, actually
null and actually Ricci-null (actual `esMetric`, `ricciOf`), where the candidate's own
Einstein–Maxwell equations hold and `f, m, N, alphaSq > 0`. VII-06's pointwise classification
(`vii06_ricci_null_directions`) puts `V(y)` on one of the two principal lines at every `y ∈ U`; it
does not say which, and no sign choice or local constancy is used. The common scale
`ρ = f V⁰ / e` then satisfies, **on the open set `U`**, the momentum identities
`(gV)₀ = -ρ p'`, `(gV)₃ = -ρ u a'`, `(gV)₄ = -ρ (1-u) a'`, which may be differentiated. With the
lowered-acceleration identity (`∂_t g = ∂_φ g = ∂_ψ g = 0`) the derivatives of `ρ` cancel in

  `p' ((g·accel V)₃ + (g·accel V)₄) - a' (g·accel V)₀ = ρ V¹ G`,

and pregeodesicity at `x` makes the left side vanish; `ρ ≠ 0`, `V¹ ≠ 0` give `G(R) = 0`
(`vii07_ricci_null_pregeodesic_G_zero`). The multiplier `κ` is never differentiated.

Composition with VII-05: `SmoothBranch.restrict` (same independent extension, smaller radius) and a
fresh VII-05 call at the smaller radius `η`. Results are labelled a **Ricci-null pregeodesic
congruence obstruction**: the Kerr–Schild ⇒ Ricci-null bridge is not part of this module. -/

